  "stemBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "P = (1 −2 / 3 4) and Q = (5 1 / −1 2). (a) Calculate 2P − Q. (b) Find the 2 × 2 zero matrix Z such that P + Z = P."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: Do the scalar multiplication first, then the subtraction — exactly the order of operations you use with numbers."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p196_q06.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p196-q06 from workbook page 196."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Multiply every entry of P by 2.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "2(1) = 2; 2(−2) = −4; 2(3) = 6; 2(4) = 8"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 2P = (2 −4 / 6 8)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Subtract each entry of Q from the matching entry of 2P.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "2 − 5 = −3; −4 − 1 = −5; 6 − (−1) = 7; 8 − 2 = 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 2P − Q = (−3 −5 / 7 6)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 3,
      "instruction": "Decide what must be added to each entry of P to leave it unchanged.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Adding 0 to any number leaves it alone, so every entry of Z must be 0."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: Z = (0 0 / 0 0)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Double every entry of P, subtract the matching entry of Q, then recall what matrix leaves P unchanged under addition."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "(a) 2P − Q = (−3 −5 / 7 6)  (b) Z = (0 0 / 0 0), the 2 × 2 zero matrix."
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Scalar multiplication is applied before addition or subtraction, just as with ordinary algebra. The zero matrix plays the same role for matrices that the number 0 plays for numbers: it is the additive identity, so adding it changes nothing. It must have the same order as P for the addition to be defined at all."
    }
  ],
